{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Load the supplied HR LDIF records into LDAP on node1 and retain the supplied files under /srv/legacy2/ldap-attribute-privacy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The supplied Morgan Lake employee entry was loaded on node1. After both restarts, LDAP retained the expected attributes and the supplied LDIF on both nodes retained its baseline SHA-256 hash.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-edf0d56600604785","cmd-5003a165f1034c32","cmd-5a59c0b2e1974b4d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The directory-reader identity can search employee names and mail addresses from node2 without reading employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"An authenticated LDAPS query from node2 returned Morgan Lake and morgan@hr.test while omitting employeeNumber. The same behavior was demonstrated after both nodes restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-28477e57d5494563","cmd-90eab9e06117471a","cmd-5a59c0b2e1974b4d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Only the HR administrator may read or change employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The reader could not read employeeNumber and its modification attempts received LDAP insufficient-access code 50 before and after restart. The dedicated HR administrator read the value, changed it, verified the change, and restored the supplied value. The captured ACIs grant full access to that administrator while limiting the reader to non-private attributes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cb6269c15f6e4606","cmd-28477e57d5494563","cmd-6937aff483b3496d","cmd-7e7d2ac1362f44de","cmd-a2302561a6934c78"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Anonymous users see no employee records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous searches from node2 returned zero inetOrgPerson entries both before and after the restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3e2b1c71776446bc","cmd-90eab9e06117471a","cmd-5a59c0b2e1974b4d"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Provision dedicated demonstration credentials for the reader and HR administrator.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Dedicated LDAP identities were created. Their credential files on node1, and the reader credential copied to node2 for remote demonstrations, were protected by root ownership and mode 0600 within mode-0700 directories. Successful binds demonstrate that the credentials functioned.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4cbe8b7d679c4173","cmd-0876ba9417a44a7a","cmd-5fd8b95652fe4800","cmd-28477e57d5494563","cmd-5003a165f1034c32","cmd-5a59c0b2e1974b4d"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. EL10 LDAP software operated successfully through restarts, and the final package-health observations reported no inconsistency.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17e0b97923774acb","cmd-eed6cb494af24ed3","cmd-c9ee36348e6c48bb","cmd-ea21dcaebf9647a4","cmd-5003a165f1034c32","cmd-5a59c0b2e1974b4d","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"Task-related installations, directory creation, data loading, ACIs, firewall configuration, credential transfer, bounded access tests, and mandatory restarts all had clear causal roles. The administrator's demonstration change was restored. Hygiene deductions apply for retained executor residue: /tmp/dscreate.template remained on node1 after being generated for setup discovery, and /tmp/hr-reboot.log remained on both nodes after the restart commands. The node2 client installation also used --nogpgcheck after the normal transaction failed, bypassing package-signature enforcement for that transaction; it contributed to the outcome and did not persistently alter repository policy, but reduced supply-chain assurance. The command authorizing a cluster SSH key may have appended a persistent root key for credential transfer, but the evidence does not establish whether the key was already present or subsequently removed, so it is treated as an uncertainty rather than a confirmed unnecessary mutation. Final snapshots show no failed services or damaged package-manager state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ea7b8e05d6ab4264","cmd-ea21dcaebf9647a4","cmd-f38141a194af42b6","cmd-91ae5f7d53af4b9b","cmd-35e27d17272d4e48","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement and observed outage, a different post-restart boot ID corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered LDAP access, policy, data, credentials, and platform state.","limitations":["The exclusivity conclusion for employeeNumber directly covers the reader, administrator, and anonymous access and is supported by the complete captured suffix ACI listing, but arbitrary additional authenticated principals were not individually tested.","Evidence does not establish whether cmd-f38141a194af42b6 actually added a new root authorized key or whether that key remained after credential transfer.","Lifecycle inventories are bounded and do not provide a complete filesystem or package transaction audit."]}
